WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:02.545
Human imagination.

2
00:00:02.845 --> 00:00:04.885
Adaptive intelligence.

3
00:00:05.185 --> 00:00:13.675
Quesar by MLAI introduces assistant workflows, memory systems and developer tools with inspectable sources.

4
00:00:15.294 --> 00:00:17.109
A place to begin.

5
00:00:17.409 --> 00:00:19.374
Read the architecture.

6
00:00:19.674 --> 00:00:26.914
The website brings products, platform, developers, research, services and contact into one navigation.

7
00:00:28.533 --> 00:00:30.123
Three roles.

8
00:00:30.423 --> 00:00:32.338
One conversation.

9
00:00:32.638 --> 00:00:36.128
Abbey is a human-facing companion contract.

10
00:00:36.428 --> 00:00:39.118
Aviva is a direct expert mode.

11
00:00:39.418 --> 00:00:43.933
Abi coordinates intent, risk, context and response style.

12
00:00:45.551 --> 00:00:47.016
Memory.

13
00:00:47.316 --> 00:00:49.031
Keep its provenance.

14
00:00:49.331 --> 00:00:57.696
WDBX local Rust storage and retrieval components preserve durable records, vectors and causal history.

15
00:00:59.315 --> 00:01:00.980
Developers.

16
00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:02.945
Start with source.

17
00:01:03.245 --> 00:01:08.610
Explore the ABI Rust framework, local CLI and MCP contracts.

18
00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:14.275
Follow setup and verification guidance before connecting tools or memory.

19
00:01:15.894 --> 00:01:17.434
Two names.

20
00:01:17.734 --> 00:01:19.549
Two distinct scopes.

21
00:01:19.849 --> 00:01:23.989
Quesar is the MLAI website and broader direction.

22
00:01:24.289 --> 00:01:29.129
Quasar is the separately configured local website builder service.

23
00:01:30.748 --> 00:01:32.163
Connect.

24
00:01:32.463 --> 00:01:34.278
Choose an origin.

25
00:01:34.578 --> 00:01:39.393
Settings lets the browser reach a local service and check that it answers.

26
00:01:39.693 --> 00:01:43.008
The deployment may supply a default origin.

27
00:01:44.626 --> 00:01:46.266
A new site.

28
00:01:46.566 --> 00:01:48.356
Begin with a prompt.

29
00:01:48.656 --> 00:01:58.871
The local service copies a Next.js template into its sites directory and runs a Claude generation job using that machine’s Anthropic credentials.

30
00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:02.180
Generation.

31
00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:04.195
Follow the feed.

32
00:02:04.495 --> 00:02:09.535
The site detail screen polls service feed and preview state every second.

33
00:02:09.835 --> 00:02:14.625
A generation is a job to inspect, not an invisible promise.

34
00:02:16.244 --> 00:02:17.734
Preview.

35
00:02:18.034 --> 00:02:19.874
A separate opening.

36
00:02:20.174 --> 00:02:27.089
Preview launch obtains a ticket and checks the returned target against the configured service before opening it.

37
00:02:28.708 --> 00:02:30.548
The future studio.

38
00:02:30.848 --> 00:02:32.913
Visual orchestration.

39
00:02:33.213 --> 00:02:43.128
MLAI Studio is a proposed workspace for visual agent design, prompt experiments and inspecting context, memory and execution.

40
00:02:44.746 --> 00:02:46.536
Build thoughtfully.

41
00:02:46.836 --> 00:02:48.776
quesar.cloud

42
00:02:49.076 --> 00:02:51.216
Explore the architecture.

43
00:02:51.516 --> 00:02:53.281
Follow the source.

44
00:02:53.581 --> 00:02:56.421
Define the evidence your project needs.

45
00:02:56.721 --> 00:02:58.911
Quesar by MLAI.
